    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0330" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/1662a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-26T19:00:00-04:00">April 26, 1937—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Refer to my telegram April 23, 6 p.m. to Consul General.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d237-f1"/> Press correspondence from Berlin states reports are
                    current that forcible dissolution of B’nai B’rith lodges in Germany were
                    precipitated by a resurgence in the United States of anti-Nazi propaganda as
                    manifested by La Guardia incident.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d237-f2"/></p>
                <p>I would like your views and any comment as to the reasons behind this step and
                    whether the attack on cultural and charitable phases marks a new departure in
                    German Government policy. Keep me advised as to developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
